\section{Rewriter Independence}

The NLI gate operates as a precision-oriented conservative filter: it sacrifices a bounded amount of recall (8.4\% false negative rate) to ensure near-zero contamination of the downstream analysis (precision $= 98.9\%$, i.e., only 1 of 88 NLI-passed pairs is flagged by the LLM as content-altered).

\paragraph{Independent validation (GPT-4o).}
An independent spot-check by GPT-4o on 100 stratified NLI decisions (50 pass, 50 fail) confirms gate reliability without same-family bias: 94\% pass agreement (47/50), with a false positive rate of 6\% (3/50).
Disagreements are overwhelmingly conservative---91\% of NLI--GPT-4o divergences (32/35) involve NLI rejecting pairs that GPT-4o accepts.
The 5pp precision gap between same-family (Qwen3-32B, 98.9\%) and independent (GPT-4o, 94\%) validation quantifies the evaluator-producer component of gate validation.

